\begin_layout Section*
Problem 7
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To create a shared library I used the g++ compiler with a -shared flag.
 Under the default target plus,
 I added the flag -Wl,-rpath,.
 to the compiler command.
 This is because during the program execution the compiler doesn't automatically check the working directory for the shared library.
 This was discussed under the 
\begin_inset Quotes eld
\end_inset

Mysterious Problems
\begin_inset Quotes erd
\end_inset

 section,
 but I didn't know if there was another standard way of fixing this problem.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Running ldd with and without the flag -Wl,-rpath,.
 the issue becomes clear
\end_layout

